        "content": "Documents give contradicting answers about the same thing. Other documents, which take no side, may state a fact that makes one of the answers impossible.\n\nQuestion: When was the National Indian Association formed?\n\nAnswer A: 1870\n  about: National Indian Association\n  sense: 1870\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"\"The \"National Indian Association in Aid of Social Progress in India\" was formed by Mary Carpenter in 1870 in Bristol.\" [document 3]; \"The National Indian Association in Aid of Social Progress in India was formed by Mary Carpenter in 1870 in Bristol.\" [document 4]\n\nAnswer B: 1879\n  about: National Indian Association\n  sense: formation year\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 2\n  evidence: \"Initially founded in 1879 in reaction to the prospect of opening Oklahoma Indian Territory to white settlement.\" [document 5]; \"Journal of the National Indian Association in 1879\" [document 6]\n\nThe other documents:\nDocument 2: Indian elected representation in legislatures. The Reform Association faction on July 26, 1876 established a \"Bharat Sabha\" with Bengali leaders like Surendranath Banerjee, Sivanath Sastri, Ananda Mohan Bose etc. and held its first annual conference in Calcutta. Initially under Sen it was pro-Crown. However, after the 2nd Brahmo Schism of 1878, the Sadharan Brahmo Samaj regrouped with Adi Brahmo Samaj to promote nationalism and freedom from British rule. From 1880 till 1890 a bitter battle for control of the Reform Association ensued between the pro-Sen and anti-Sen factions. After the death of Sen in 1884 the Reform Association also passed. The National Indian Association was formed on January 1, 1900, as a response to growing nationalist sentiments and the need for a unified voice against British colonial policies.\n\nLook in the other documents for a fact that rules one answer out: a date of birth that makes a person too young, for example, or a plain statement that the answer is false. Use only what these documents say, nothing you know from elsewhere. A fact that only makes an answer less likely does not count.\n\nReply with JSON only. If such a fact is there:\n{\"reason\": \"one sentence\", \"impossible\": \"A\", \"document\": 1, \"quote\": \"\"}\n\"impossible\" is the letter of the answer that is ruled out. \"quote\" is the sentence stating the fact, copied word for word, and \"document\" is the number of the document it is in.\nIf there is none:\n{\"impossible\": null}\n\nInside a JSON string, write a double quote as \\\"."
